# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree on EVERY platform.
#
# Without this, the windows-latest CI runner checks files out with CRLF
# (Git's autocrlf=true default on Windows), and `biome check .` then flags a
# stray carriage return on every file — failing `pnpm check`. Forcing LF keeps
# the working tree consistent with the macOS/Linux runners (and with biome's
# default `lf` lineEnding) regardless of host OS.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect text vs binary; the explicit `binary` rules
# below protect the committed binary assets from any normalization.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.dmg   binary
